    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/casual-academics-nursing-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-unisc-caboolture-unisc-gympie-unisc-fraser-coast-unisc-thompson-institute-sunshine-coast-health-instit": {
      "title": "Casual Academics (Nursing)",
      "description": "Casual Academics (Nursing) - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia - UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia - UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia - UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Thompson Institute, QLD, Australia - Sunshine Coast Health Institute, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Casual Academics (Nursing) Sunshine Coast Health Institute, QLD, Australia, 4575 UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia, 4510 UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia, 4655 UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia, 4570 UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 UniSC Thompson Institute, QLD, Australia, 4575 UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Show More Show Less Academic Casual Academic Nursing School of Health Show More Show Less Casual Add to favourites View favourites School of Health | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Thompson Institute, Sunshine Coast Health Institute, UniSC Moreton Bay, UniSC Caboolture, UniSC Gympie and UniSC Fraser Coast Casual Academic (Nursing), rates vary depending on academic activity and classification Multiple casual opportunities commencing in 2027 The Opportunity Shape the future of Nursing education with UniSC. The School of Health at UniSC is seeking experienced and passionate Nursing professionals to join our Casual Academic team in 2027. If you are interested in contributing to the education of future nurses and value the flexibility of casual academic work, we invite you to apply. Our Nursing programs are recognised for producing graduates who are prepared to meet the evolving healthcare needs of regional, national, and global communities. We are committed to excellence in teaching, learning, research, and industry engagement, and we value educators who can bring contemporary clinical expertise and real-world insights into the classroom. As a Casual Academic in Nursing, you may contribute to a range of teaching and learning activities across undergraduate and postgraduate nursing programs. This may include tutorials, laboratory and simulation classes, clinical education support, workshops, online learning activities, and assessment across our campuses and learning environments. You will deliver high-quality teaching and learning experiences for nursing students across a range of learning environments; facilitate tutorials, laboratory and simulation activities, clinical education support, workshops and other teaching activities; assess and mark student work in accordance with University standards, providing timely and constructive feedback to support student learning and success; and contribute to an inclusive and positive learning environment, maintaining contemporary nursing knowledge and engaging professionally with academic colleagues, clinical partners and students. About you We’re looking for experienced and passionate Nursing professionals who are committed to supporting the education and development of future nurses. You’ll bring contemporary nursing knowledge and professional experience to your teaching, with the ability to engage students and create positive and inclusive learning environments. You’ll be a strong communicator who can work collaboratively with academic colleagues and clinical partners while supporting high-quality teaching, learning and assessment. You will possess: Current registration as a Registered Nurse with AHPRA. A relevant postgraduate qualification in a health-related field. Experience in teaching, tutoring or academic assessment at a tertiary level. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage and inspire students. Ability to assess student work and provide timely, constructive feedback. Evidence of professional development and maintaining contemporary knowledge and practice in the health field. Ability to work collaboratively with academic colleagues, clinical partners and students. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Saturday 7 November 2026. Your completed application must include: a resume , which will be reviewed in alignment with the specified selection criteria outlined in this advertisement. You will also have the opportunity to attach further supporting documentation should you wish. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:34 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:34 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) 46cc1aff Last Name (required) 9613552a Email (required) a9cc56b6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / 