    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/eoi-administration-support-talent-pool-unisc-fraser-coast-qld-australia-unisc-sunshine-coast-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-unisc-caboolture-unisc-gympie-unisc-southbank-unisc-thompson-institut": {
      "title": "EOI: Administration Support talent pool",
      "description": "EOI: Administration Support talent pool - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia - UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia - UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia - UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC SouthBank, QLD, Australia - UniSC Thompson Institute, QLD, Australia - Sunshine Coast Health Institute, QLD, Australia - Health Hub Morayfield, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES EOI: Administration Support talent pool Health Hub Morayfield, QLD, Australia, 4506 Sunshine Coast Health Institute, QLD, Australia, 4575 UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia, 4510 UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia, 4655 UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia, 4570 UniSC SouthBank, QLD, Australia, 4101 UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 UniSC Thompson Institute, QLD, Australia, 4575 UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Show More Show Less Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Casual Professional Casual Add to favourites View favourites Casual staff - Administration Support Discover opportunities for casual employment in various administrative support capacities across our departments! Interested in exploring suitable roles aligned with your expertise? Express your interest to join our professional community when suitable opportunities arise. In these roles, you will have the opportunity to work alongside dedicated academics and professionals within departments such as: Executive Student administration People and Culture Finance Library Services Centre for Support and Advancement of Learning and Teaching (curriculum design and blended learning) Marketing Research Thompson Institute Facilities Management Information Technology Insights and Analytics International Office Indigenous Services Governance and Risk Management (governance, policy, compliance, risk management) Our administrative support team plays a crucial role in maintaining the operational excellence of UniSC, assisting various departments and ensuring smooth administrative processes. These roles offer diverse opportunities to contribute to the effective functioning of the university and support the academic and professional success of our community. Primary Objectives: Provide comprehensive administrative support to academic and professional staff across various departments. Assist in the preparation and distribution of documents, reports, and communications. Manage schedules, appointments, and travel arrangements for staff members. Support event planning and coordination, including meetings, workshops, and conferences. Maintain accurate and up-to-date records and databases, ensuring data integrity and confidentiality. Respond to inquiries from students, staff, and external stakeholders, providing accurate information and assistance. Contribute to the development and implementation of administrative procedures and policies. Desirable Qualifications or Skills: Proven experience in an administrative support role, preferably within an educational institution. Strong organisational and time management skills, with the ability to handle multiple tasks and deadlines. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and other relevant software. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Attention to detail and a commitment to accuracy. A proactive and customer focused approach to problem solving. If you're ready to be part of a forward-thinking institution dedicated to making a difference in education and research, we encourage you to register your interest in joining our administrative teams. Working towards a better tomorrow We're all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. We’re not the biggest university. But we’re growing every day, and doing big things. Like ground-breaking research, championing sustainability, producing gold-winning athletes and award-winning alumni. We're one of the fastest growing universities in Australia, growing to over 2,000 people across 5 campuses in South East Queensland. Teaching excellence is at the heart of what we do, and our commitment to sustainability is integrated into our teaching, research, and daily operations. According to the 2023-24 Good Universities Guide we are Australia's highest rated public university for postgraduate teaching quality, skills development and student support and Australia's number one public university for overall postgraduate student experience. Our research tackles the most pressing challenges of our time, with 26 research fields ranked at or above world standard according to the Excellence in Research for Australia Rankings. In 2023 we recorded the biggest improvement in Australia for research quality, moving up more than 331 places in the world rank. At UniSC you will have the opportunity to shape the educational landscape and inspire the minds of future generations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment, encouraging continuous professional development and providing resources to enhance your teaching and research endeavours. We recognise and value the contributions of each team member to our culture and success. We're not afraid to be different, and we're looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team that is working together to improve our local and global challenges. Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. EAP & discounted private health. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at https://www.linkedin.com/school/university-of-the-sunshine-coast/life Please note: To maintain currency of this register, applicants will be notified via email when the pool will be re-advertised, with a link to re-apply if you wish to be considered for future opportunities. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:47 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:47 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your applicati