    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/associate-professor-in-occupational-therapy-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Associate Professor in Occupational Therapy - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Associate Professor in Occupational Therapy UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Academic LD $174,423 - $192,092 +17% super School of Health Full-Time School of Heath, Sunshine Coast Campus, Sippy Downs Level D, $174,423 - $192,092 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, ongoing appointment The Opportunity Where Passion Meets Impact - Join the School of Health! Are you eager to make a difference in health education and research? Join our dedicated team of researchers and educators at the School of Health (SOH). We have a strong focus on cultivating healthy minds, bodies, and environments through our teaching, research, and outreach efforts. With a purpose that extends regionally and impacts globally, we are committed to advancing knowledge in the health sector and improving the well-being of our communities. Together, let's create healthier communities now and for the generations to come. Join UniSC as an Associate Professor in Occupational Therapy and help shape the future of the discipline through impactful teaching, research and community engagement. You’ll bring an established research profile, provide leadership and mentorship to colleagues, and build on strong professional networks across the occupational therapy sector, both locally and nationally. This is an opportunity to contribute your expertise, support the next generation of occupational therapy professionals and strengthen the impact of our work across the communities we serve. For more information, please visit us online: School of Health You will: demonstrate national standing in teaching, research or engagement, contributing to UniSC’s reputation and impact; lead impactful research, secure external funding, mentor researchers and advance the discipline nationally and internationally; deliver excellent teaching, develop innovative curricula and inspire students and colleagues; and build productive industry, government and community partnerships while contributing to University development, governance and a positive academic culture. About you: Our ideal candidate is a respected academic who brings a strong track record in research, a genuine commitment to student success and a passion for making a meaningful difference through occupational therapy. You’re ready to grow your research profile, build valuable partnerships across industry and the community, and share your expertise to shape the next generation of practitioners. With your leadership, collaborative approach and commitment to inclusive, high-quality teaching, you’ll help strengthen our discipline, support your colleagues and contribute to positive outcomes for the communities we serve. You will possess: A strong record of contributing to the advancement of your discipline, with recognised impact and influence. An established research profile, with high-quality outputs, demonstrated research impact, successful HDR supervision and external recognition of your achievements. Proven research leadership, including mentoring emerging researchers, building research capability and contributing to a positive research culture. A commitment to teaching excellence, with experience in research-led curriculum development, improving learning and teaching practices, and supporting student engagement and success. The leadership qualities to foster a positive, inclusive and collaborative academic environment where staff and students can thrive. Extensive experience and success in academic administration and contributing to University priorities. The ability to build productive regional, national and international partnerships that deliver meaningful outcomes for students, the University and our communities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. Position description: 494908_Associate Professor in Occupational Therapy.pdf UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 15 November 2026 Your completed application must include: a resume, and a response to selection criteria. Noting that within the application form, we will request a statement addressing each of the selection criteria contained within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Professor Pamela Meredith Discipline Lead, Occupational Therapy Phone: 07 5456 3875 Email: pmeredith@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Director, Insights and Analytics UniSC Sunshine Coast Director, Insights and Analytics Unit, Management, People leadership, Professional, Senior staff Lead enterprise data and analytics, shaping the evidence, capability and strategic decisions that will help us thrive and deliver a sustainable future Senior IT Systems Analyst (ERP) UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, Information Technology, L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super, Professional Shape UniSC’s digital future by delivering innovative ERP solutions, solving complex business challenges and improving systems for our university community. Clinical Trials Associate - Laboratory Health Hub Morayfield Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Professional Help bring leading-edge clinical research to life by ensuring every sample tells a story. Join a growing clinical trials operation making a real difference to health outcomes across the region. First Nations Project Support Officer (Identified Position) UniSC Sunshine Coast Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, Administration / Admin Support, Casual Professional, L4 $50.41per hour (casual), School of Health Casual role supporting scholarship promotion, stakeholder engagement, marketing and events for First Nations nurses in aged care. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candi