    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/clinical-trials-associate-laboratory-health-hub-morayfield-qld-australia-c0f3076a-ef5c-4424-a698-6a507a857ce5": {
      "title": "Clinical Trials Associate",
      "description": "Clinical Trials Associate - Laboratory - Health Hub Morayfield, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Clinical Trials Associate - Laboratory Health Hub Morayfield, QLD, Australia, 4506 Clinical Trials Individual contributor L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Professional Show More Show Less Full-Time UniSC Clinical Trials | Health Hub Morayfield Level 5, $82,843 - $93,358 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time (36.25 hours per week), 2 year fixed-term appointment The Opportunity You will play a key role in supporting the safe, compliant and efficient management of laboratory samples across a diverse portfolio of clinical trials. Working closely with laboratory and clinical trial colleagues, you will help ensure samples are collected, processed, documented, stored and shipped in line with study protocols, regulatory requirements and industry best practice. This is an excellent opportunity for an organised laboratory professional who enjoys working in a fast-paced research environment and wants to contribute to the delivery of high-quality clinical research that improves lives and strengthens healthcare outcomes. Please note , this role requires flexibility to travel to different clinical trial sites, and to work outside standard business hours to support confinement studies and other time-sensitive trial activities. You may also be required to participate in a 24/7 on-call or confinement roster. For more information, please visit us online: UniSC Clinical Trials You will Support the Laboratory Manager and Clinical Trials Co-ordinator with the management of laboratory samples collected, processed, and shipped for trials conducted at UniSC Clinical Trials (UniSC CT);  and Work collaboratively with the UniSC CT team, sponsors, and monitors to ensure appropriate and timely management of all trial protocol nominated laboratory samples. About you You have a strong grasp of ICH Good Clinical Practice and Good Laboratory Practice, with proven experience ensuring compliance with regulations. Skilled in using databases, electronic data entry systems, and standard office software, you adapt quickly and make an immediate impact in clinical trial laboratories or similar settings. You work effectively both independently and within multidisciplinary teams, thriving in collaborative environments while bringing a proactive, detail-oriented, and solutions-focused approach. You will possess: Completion of a Degree qualification in Health Science/Bio-Medical Science and relevant laboratory experience – or a combination of relevant work experience and education/training; Knowledge of ICH Good Clinical Practice/ Good Laboratory Practice and applicable regulations; High level computing skills (including databases, clinical trial electronic data entry, word processing and spreadsheets); Previous experience in a clinical trial laboratory role/setting will be highly regarded; Ability to work independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team; and Current Safe Transport Infectious Substances by Air certification highly regarded. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 1 November 2026. Position description: 494930_Clinical Trials Associate - Laboratory.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Stefan Sonderegger Laboratory Manager - UniSC Clinical Trials Telephone: 07 5456 3880 Email: ssonderegger@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Director, Insights and Analytics UniSC Sunshine Coast Director, Insights and Analytics Unit, Management, People leadership, Professional, Senior staff Lead enterprise data and analytics, shaping the evidence, capability and strategic decisions that will help us thrive and deliver a sustainable future Associate Professor in Occupational Therapy UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic, LD $174,423 - $192,092 +17% super, School of Health Shape the future of occupational therapy at UniSC, where your research, teaching and leadership can make a lasting difference for students, the profession and the communities we serve. Senior IT Systems Analyst (ERP) UniSC Sunshine Coast Individual contributor, Information Technology, L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super, Professional Shape UniSC’s digital future by delivering innovative ERP solutions, solving complex business challenges and improving systems for our university community. First Nations Project Support Officer (Identified Position) UniSC Sunshine Coast Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, Administration / Admin Support, Casual Professional, L4 $50.41per hour (casual), School of Health Casual role supporting scholarship promotion, stakeholder engagement, marketing and events for First Nations nurses in aged care. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I