    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/eoi-campus-development-and-services-talent-pool-unisc-fraser-coast-qld-australia-unisc-sunshine-coast-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-unisc-caboolture-unisc-gympie": {
      "title": "EOI: Campus Development and Services talent pool",
      "description": "EOI: Campus Development and Services talent pool - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia - UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia - UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia - UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES EOI: Campus Development and Services talent pool UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia, 4510 UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia, 4655 UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia, 4570 UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Show More Show Less Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Casual Professional Casual Casual staff – Campus Development and Services Discover opportunities for casual employment within UniSC’s Campus Development and Services team! Interested in exploring suitable roles aligned with your expertise? Express your interest to join our community when suitable opportunities arise. Our Campus Development and Services team is dedicated to ensuring a safe, efficient, and inviting environment for the entire UniSC community. These roles encompass a variety of functions such as building maintenance, groundskeeping, custodial services, and facility planning, all aimed at supporting the university’s operational excellence. Primary Objectives: Perform routine maintenance and repairs on university buildings, systems, and equipment to ensure their optimal functioning. General groundskeeping duties, including landscaping, gardening, and exterior maintenance. Coordinate custodial services to maintain cleanliness and hygiene across all facilities. Assist in facility planning and project management for new constructions, renovations, and space optimisation. Contribute to environmental sustainability initiatives to reduce the university’s ecological footprint. Ensure compliance with health, safety, and environmental regulations, conducting regular inspections and risk assessments. Provide exceptional customer service by promptly addressing and resolving facility related issues reported by students, staff, and visitors. Desirable Qualifications or Skills: Experience in facilities management, building maintenance, or a related field. Relevant trade qualifications or certifications (e.g., electrical, plumbing, HVAC). Strong problem solving skills with the ability to troubleshoot and resolve maintenance issues efficiently. Excellent organisational and time management abilities. Knowledge of health, safety, and environmental regulations and best practices. Proficiency in using maintenance management software and tools. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with a customer focused approach. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Join us in our mission to maintain and enhance UniSC's physical infrastructure to support teaching, learning, and research. If you're dedicated to excellence in facilities management and ready to contribute your skills and expertise, we encourage you to register your expression of interest. Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. EAP & discounted private health. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. Contact People and Culture for further information : UniSC-careers@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at https://www.linkedin.com/school/university-of-the-sunshine-coast/life Please note: To maintain currency of this register, applicants will be notified via email when the pool will be re-advertised, with a link to re-apply if you wish to be considered for future opportunities. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:47 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:47 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) 434db66a Last Name (required) da6fb12f Email (required) 8b67ceab Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you About UniSC For more in