    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/international-business-development-coordinator-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-9d599c2b-c229-490b-8179-c73211f49332": {
      "title": "International Business Development Coordinator",
      "description": "International Business Development Coordinator - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES International Business Development Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Individual contributor International L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super Professional Show More Show Less Full-Time International | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs or UniSC Moreton Bay, Petrie Level 6, $95,986 - $103,873 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time (36.25 hours per week), Ongoing appointment The Opportunity In this role, you’ll play a key part in driving UniSC’s international student recruitment success, supporting targeted strategies that turn market opportunities into student commencements and revenue growth. With a primary focus on the onshore market and support for offshore recruitment across all regions, you’ll use market intelligence to identify growth opportunities, maximise return on investment and advance UniSC’s global ambitions. Drawing on your knowledge of international education pathways, qualifications and emerging market trends, you’ll help strengthen education agent performance, boost enquiry-to-enrolment conversion and deliver effective recruitment support. Through strong stakeholder partnerships, data-informed insights and a proactive approach, you’ll help grow UniSC’s international presence and achieve measurable recruitment outcomes. Please note – This role requires regular non-standard working hours, with potential restrictions on recreational leave during peak periods. Regular domestic travel and occasional international travel will also be required. For more information, please visit us online: International You will Contribute to the development and implementation of market-specific international student recruitment strategies for allocated regions, regularly monitoring, reviewing and reporting on performance and return on investment. Maintain up-to-date knowledge of international education pathways, academic qualifications, and market trends and provide regular insights and detailed reports on market conditions and strategic growth opportunities. Build and sustain strong, productive relationships with key stakeholders and oversee performance and training of education agents. About you You’re a proactive, results-driven professional with sharp analytical skills and the ability to turn market intelligence and performance data into strategic insights. You thrive under pressure, meet tight deadlines, achieve targets and confidently solve problems independently. Your exceptional stakeholder engagement, relationship-building and cross-cultural collaboration skills enable you to build influential partnerships and represent the University with confidence. With outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, you bring people together, work seamlessly across teams and champion the University’s brand and reputation. You will possess: Expert knowledge of international student recruitment and/or admissions practices and ability to interpret and apply relevant policies and procedures; Analytical skills, with the ability to gather, interpret and report on market intelligence and performance data to inform strategic decisions; Ability to understand and interpret a range of source-country education systems, academic qualifications and factors influencing student decisions; Ability to identify and effectively respond to areas of operational risk in an agile manner; and Demonstrated understanding of the Australian and international Higher Education sector including current issues and emerging trends in the governance and internationalisation of Higher Education. Desirable Fluency in a language other than English and of relevance to the regions of responsibility. Experience and expertise in the use of a CRM and Eloqua. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Monday 9 November 2026. Position description: 494983_International Business Development Coordinator.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Sam Poulton Associate Director, International (Business Development) - International Telephone: 07 5456 5202 Email: spoulton@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Finance Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast Financial Services, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Professional Partner with senior leaders to shape financial decisions that directly support UniSC’s strategy, growth and sustainability. Senior Lecturer in Prosthetics and Orthotics UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic, LC $144,979 - $167,068 +17% super, School of Health An exceptional opportunity to shape the future of prosthetics and orthotics education, advance impactful research, and strengthen partnerships with clinical and industry leaders at a university committed to innovation and real-world impact. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Fraser Coast Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. Technician, Nutrition and Dietetics UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support An exciting opportunity to support innovative health education through specialised technical expertise, high-quality practical learning experiences, and the safe and effective operation of teaching facilities at UniSC. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
