    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-in-prosthetics-and-orthotics-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Prosthetics and Orthotics",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer in Prosthetics and Orthotics - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Senior Lecturer in Prosthetics and Orthotics UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Academic LC $144,979 - $167,068 +17% super School of Health Full-Time School of Health, UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs Level C, $144,979 - $167,068 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, ongoing appointment with relocation assistance available for eligible candidates relocating to the region SOH: Where Passion Meets Impact - Join the School of Health! Are you eager to make a difference in health education and research? Join our dedicated team of researchers and educators at the School of Health (SOH). We have a strong focus on cultivating healthy minds, bodies, and environments through our teaching, research, and outreach efforts. With a purpose that extends regionally and impacts globally, we are committed to advancing knowledge in the health sector and improving the well-being of our communities. Together, let's create healthier communities now and for the generations to come. The Opportunity As a Senior Lecturer in Prosthetics and Orthotics, you will play a pivotal role in shaping the future of the Bachelor of Prosthetics and Orthotics program. You will provide academic leadership in curriculum development and renewal, deliver innovative and engaging teaching, and support the development of highly skilled, work-ready graduates equipped to address complex clinical challenges and provide person-centred care. You will also contribute to the growth of the program’s research profile, building collaborative partnerships with clinical providers, industry and professional organisations to advance research, innovation and clinical practice. This is an opportunity to influence the ongoing development of prosthetics and orthotics education at UniSC, strengthen industry connections and contribute to the long-term success of a growing program. For more information on the School of Health, please visit us online: School of Health You will: provide academic leadership in the development, delivery and continuous improvement of contemporary prosthetics and orthotics curricula; deliver high-quality teaching, assessment and clinical education that supports student engagement, learning and professional readiness; develop and contribute to impactful research, including publications, competitive grant applications, collaborative projects and higher degree research supervision; and build productive partnerships with clinical providers, industry, professional bodies and community stakeholders to strengthen student learning, research collaboration and professional engagement. About you You are an experienced prosthetics and orthotics professional and accomplished academic with a passion for advancing education, research and clinical practice. You bring a strong understanding of the profession and the ability to translate your clinical expertise into engaging, contemporary learning experiences that prepare students for complex and evolving healthcare environments. You are a collaborative and forward-thinking academic who can provide leadership in curriculum development, contribute to a growing research profile and build meaningful partnerships across the profession. You are committed to academic excellence, continuous improvement and creating a positive learning and working environment for students and colleagues. You will possess: A minimum of ten years' clinical experience as an accredited professional in the field of prosthetics and orthotics; Completion or near-completion of a PhD in a relevant field, or equivalent accreditation and standing; Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching, including the ability to develop, deliver and evaluate higher education curricula and contribute to teaching leadership; An established record of research activity, including peer-reviewed publications, research collaboration, external grant participation, higher degree research supervision and demonstrated research impact; Demonstrated leadership, interpersonal and organisational skills, with the ability to contribute to a positive academic culture, undertake academic administration and build productive relationships with professional, clinical and industry stakeholders; and A commitment to ongoing academic and professional development, with a demonstrated willingness to reflect on practice and continually improve teaching, research and engagement outcomes. Desirable Professional experience as a Prosthetist Orthotist Postgraduate qualifications in higher education Recognition for excellence in teaching and/or research. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 15 November 2026. Position Description: 494861_Senior Lecturer in Prosthetics and Orthotics.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume , and a response to selection criteria . Noting that within the application form, we will request a statement addressing each of the selection criteria contained within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Associate Professor Jane Taylor Discipline Lead, Public Health - School of Health Telephone: +61 7 5459 4543 Email: jtaylor6@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you International Business Development Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Individual contributor, International , L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super, Professional Support UniSC’s international recruitment success by delivering targeted onshore strategies, strengthening education agent partnerships and building pathways that attract international students and convert opportunities into enrolments. Finance Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast Financial Services, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Professional Partner with senior leaders to shape financial decisions that directly support UniSC’s strategy, growth and sustainability. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Fraser Coast Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. Technician, Nutrition and Dietetics UniSC Moreton Bay Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support An exciting opportunity to support innovative health education through specialised technical expertise, high-quality practical learning experiences, and the safe and effective operation of teaching facilities at UniSC. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings