    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-in-occupational-therapy-clinical-education-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia-d21c066f-ded1-45e1-8297-d21827d95c30": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Occupational Therapy",
      "description": "Lecturer in Occupational Therapy - Clinical Education - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Lecturer in Occupational Therapy - Clinical Education UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Academic Individual contributor LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super School of Health Show More Show Less Part-Time School of Health | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs Level B, $118,481 - $140,567 p.a (pro rata)., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Part-time, (20%FTE, 7.25 hours per week), Ongoing appointment The School of Health (SOH) Where Passion Meets Impact - Join the School of Health! Are you eager to make a difference in health education and research? Join our dedicated team of researchers and educators at the School of Health (SOH). We have a strong focus on cultivating healthy minds, bodies, and environments through our teaching, research, and outreach efforts. With a purpose that extends regionally and impacts globally, we are committed to advancing knowledge in the health sector and improving the well-being of our communities. Together, let's create healthier communities now and for the generations to come. The opportunity You’ll play a key role in supporting Occupational Therapy students to develop the clinical skills, confidence and professional capability they need to thrive in practice. Working under the broad direction of the Discipline Lead, Occupational Therapy, you’ll contribute to clinical teaching, student placement experiences and the development of a sustainable professional placement program, while building strong partnerships with healthcare providers, community organisations and industry stakeholders. Join a collaborative team committed to innovative learning experiences, strong community connections and positive student outcomes across simulated, telehealth, internal and external clinical placements. Please note , this position role is located at the UniSC Sunshine Coast campus at Sippy Downs and may require travel to different locations. For more information, please visit us online: School of Health You will: Deliver engaging clinical education and learning experiences across occupational therapy programs. Lead and support quality placement experiences, including simulated, telehealth, internal and external placements. Assess student learning and provide constructive feedback that supports growth and professional readiness. Work collaboratively with colleagues to strengthen placement opportunities and student learning pathways. Build and maintain productive relationships with healthcare providers, professional bodies, community organisations and industry partners. Contribute to governance, school initiatives and activities that enhance the student experience. Integrate scholarship, professional practice and research-informed approaches into teaching and learning. About you: You’re an experienced occupational therapy professional who is passionate about developing future practitioners and supporting student success. Whether your background is in clinical practice, clinical education, higher education or a combination of these areas, you’ll bring professional credibility, collaboration and a commitment to quality learning experiences. You’ll enjoy building relationships, identifying opportunities for innovation and working with diverse stakeholders, while confidently mentoring students, contributing to team initiatives and strengthening partnerships across the profession. You will possess: Completion of a Masters or PhD qualification; or near-completion of a PhD qualification; in a relevant field or equivalent accreditation and standing or a minimum of ten years clinical experience as an accredited profession in the field of study; Effectiveness as a teacher, which is evidenced by: student feedback on clinical teaching and student supervision placement in various forms: including simulated placement, telehealth placement, external and internal placements using valid instrument/s, peer review and/or student outcomes, and the capacity to conceive, develop and deliver higher education curricula and contribute to relevant areas of teaching. Evidence of leadership of quality clinical education of undergraduate students in various forms: including simulated, telehealth, external and internal placements; Membership of and sound connections with relevant professional bodies, community groups and/or in professional practice and evidence of leading development of new partnerships; Strong personal qualities and collegial approaches that contribute to the development and maintenance of a positive academic environment which is conducive to high levels of engagement and standards of achievement for both staff and students and evidence of leading staff; and Evidence of participation in academic development activities and the desire to continue to learn and improve as an effective academic. Desirable Experience undertaking academic administrative functions (e.g., course coordination), within a University. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 15 November 2026. Position description: 494909_Lecturer in Occupational Therapy - Clinical Education.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Professor Pamela Meredith Discipline Lead, Occupational Therapy – School of Health Telephone: 07 5456 3875 Email: pmeredith@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you International Business Development Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Individual contributor, International , L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super, Professional Support UniSC’s international recruitment success by delivering targeted onshore strategies, strengthening education agent partnerships and building pathways that attract international students and convert opportunities into enrolments. Finance Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast Financial Services, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Professional Partner with senior leaders to shape financial decisions that directly support UniSC’s strategy, growth and sustainability. Senior Lecturer in Prosthetics and Orthotics UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic, LC $144,979 - $167,068 +17% super, School of Health An exceptional opportunity to shape the future of prosthetics and orthotics education, advance impactful research, and strengthen partnerships with clinical and industry leaders at a university committed to innovation and real-world impact. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Fraser Coast Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If 