    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/marketing-and-communications-coordinator-business-short-courses-project-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Marketing and Communications Coordinator (Business Short Courses Project)",
      "description": "Marketing and Communications Coordinator (Business Short Courses Project) - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Marketing and Communications Coordinator (Business Short Courses Project) UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Individual contributor L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super School of Business and Creative Industries Full-Time School of Business and Creative Industries | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs Level 6, $95,986 - $103,873 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time (36.25 hours per week), fixed term appointment until June 2029 The Opportunity Join UniSC and use your marketing and communications expertise to make a meaningful impact on Queensland’s business community. The School of Business and Creative Industries is seeking a creative and collaborative Marketing and Communications Coordinator to support the promotion and delivery of a four-year Queensland Government-funded Business Short Courses Project. Building on six years of successful course delivery, the project provides a suite of short courses designed to build business capability and support long-term sustainability across Queensland. In this role, you will coordinate marketing campaigns, develop engaging creative and digital content, monitor campaign performance and collaborate with UniSC Marketing and Communications, the funding partner and external stakeholders to drive course awareness, participant registrations and engagement. For more information, please visit us online: School of Business and Creative Industries You will contribute to the development and implementation of marketing and communications plans and campaigns that increase course awareness, registrations and engagement across Queensland; coordinate the development and delivery of creative assets, digital and print materials, web content and promotional activities, ensuring consistent messaging, branding and accessibility; and monitor and evaluate campaign performance, enrolment and engagement data, providing insights and recommendations to improve marketing effectiveness and project outcomes. About you You are a proactive and creative marketing and communications professional with experience developing and delivering campaigns across a range of channels. You bring strong digital marketing and content development skills, with the ability to coordinate marketing activities, monitor performance against objectives and use data to inform improvements. You are a confident communicator who builds productive relationships with internal and external stakeholders, manages competing priorities and takes initiative to solve problems. You enjoy working collaboratively, adapting to changing priorities and contributing fresh ideas to achieve meaningful outcomes. Experience in higher education, working with government or supporting small businesses will be highly regarded. You will possess: A relevant degree in marketing, communications or a related field, with subsequent relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant work experience and education or training; Demonstrated experience developing, implementing and evaluating marketing and communications plans and campaigns within approved budgets to achieve key performance indicators and objectives; Experience developing marketing materials and creative assets for a range of channels and audiences, including digital, print, web and social media, with knowledge of performance media and digital advertising optimisation; Strong analytical and reporting skills, with the ability to interpret campaign data, evaluate performance, identify opportunities and recommend improvements; Well-developed problem-solving, organisational and communication skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, adapt approaches and deliver positive outcomes; and Demonstrated stakeholder engagement and relationship-building skills, including negotiation skills and the ability to work independently and collaboratively. Experience in higher education, working with Queensland small businesses or government agencies, and graphic design will be highly regarded. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 8 November 2026. Position Description: 494935_Marketing and Communications Coordinator.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume, which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. There will be the opportunity to attach further documentation for consideration should you wish. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Wayne Graham Senior Lecturer in Management Telephone: 07 5430 1287 Email: wgraham@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you International Business Development Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Individual contributor, International , L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super, Professional Support UniSC’s international recruitment success by delivering targeted onshore strategies, strengthening education agent partnerships and building pathways that attract international students and convert opportunities into enrolments. Finance Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast Financial Services, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Professional Partner with senior leaders to shape financial decisions that directly support UniSC’s strategy, growth and sustainability. Senior Lecturer in Prosthetics and Orthotics UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic, LC $144,979 - $167,068 +17% super, School of Health An exceptional opportunity to shape the future of prosthetics and orthotics education, advance impactful research, and strengthen partnerships with clinical and industry leaders at a university committed to innovation and real-world impact. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Fraser Coast Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
