    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/regional-partnerships-advisor-business-short-courses-project-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Regional Partnerships Advisor (Business Short Courses Project)",
      "description": "Regional Partnerships Advisor (Business Short Courses Project) - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Regional Partnerships Advisor (Business Short Courses Project) UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Individual contributor L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super School of Business and Creative Industries Full-Time School of Business and Creative Industries | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs Level 7 $105,843 - $115,703 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time (36.25 hours per week), fixed term appointment until June 2029 The Opportunity The School of Business and Creative Industries is seeking an experienced and relationship-focused Regional Partnerships Advisor to support the delivery and success of the Business Short Courses Project, a Queensland Government-funded initiative helping businesses across Queensland build capability and long-term sustainability through practical learning and development. This is an exciting opportunity to strengthen UniSC’s connections with regional business communities, increase awareness and participation in the program, and contribute to meaningful outcomes for small and family businesses across the state. Working under the broad direction of the Academic Lead, you will develop and implement stakeholder engagement strategies, establish strategic partnerships and build productive relationships with business and industry leaders, government representatives and regional networks. You will provide expert advice and market intelligence to inform program planning, represent UniSC at regional forums and stakeholder meetings, and collaborate with government, academic, project and marketing teams to increase course registrations and maximise the impact of the initiative. For more information, please visit us online: School of Business and Creative Industries You will develop and implement stakeholder engagement and partnership strategies that strengthen regional connections, increase program awareness and drive participation in business short courses; establish and maintain productive relationships with government representatives, business and industry networks, community organisations and regional stakeholders to support program objectives; analyse regional trends, stakeholder insights and participation data to identify opportunities, inform decision-making and support continuous improvement; and represent UniSC at stakeholder meetings and regional events, providing expert advice, briefing materials and reports to support engagement outcomes and program performance. About you You are a proactive and strategic relationship builder who enjoys connecting people, identifying opportunities and developing partnerships that deliver meaningful outcomes. With experience in business development, stakeholder engagement or partnership management, you are confident engaging with industry and government stakeholders and building trusted professional relationships across diverse regional communities. You bring strong communication, facilitation and negotiation skills, together with the ability to analyse complex information, identify risks and opportunities, and develop practical solutions. You are adaptable, comfortable working autonomously and skilled at influencing and collaborating with stakeholders to achieve shared objectives. An understanding of the higher education sector and the role of universities in delivering non-credit-bearing short courses will be highly regarded. You will possess: A relevant qualification, together with at least four years’ subsequent experience in business development within an industry or university environment. Demonstrated experience developing and implementing stakeholder engagement, partnership development or business development strategies, with a proven track record of establishing collaborative relationships with industry and government. Strong facilitation, negotiation and influencing skills, with the ability to build productive relationships and achieve outcomes without direct authority. Proven analytical and problem-solving skills, including the ability to assess risks, benefits and opportunities, analyse stakeholder and market trends, and develop practical recommendations. Excellent interpersonal, communication and report-writing skills, including experience preparing proposals, briefing materials and planning documents to support strategic engagement and partnership outcomes. An understanding of the higher education sector, industry engagement and emerging opportunities in university–industry collaboration, together with the flexibility and adaptability to respond to changing priorities and regional stakeholder needs. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 8 November 2026. Position Description: 494936_Regional Partnerships Advisor.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume and a statement of suitability (not to exceed two pages), which will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Wayne Graham Senior Lecturer in Management Telephone: 07 5430 1287 Email: wgraham@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green