    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-in-mental-health-nursing-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia-unisc-caboolture": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Mental Health Nursing",
      "description": "Lecturer in Mental Health Nursing - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Lecturer in Mental Health Nursing UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia, 4510 UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Academic LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super School of Health Full-Time School of Health | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs or UniSC Caboolture Academic Level B - $118,481 - $140,567 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, ongoing appointment | Relocation assistance available for eligible candidates SOH: Where Passion Meets Impact - Join the School of Health! Are you eager to make a difference in health education and research? Join our dedicated team of researchers and educators at the School of Health (SOH). We have a strong focus on cultivating healthy minds, bodies, and environments through our teaching, research, and outreach efforts. With a purpose that extends regionally and impacts globally, we are committed to advancing knowledge in the health sector and improving the well-being of our communities. Together, let's create healthier communities now and for the generations to come. The Opportunity As a Lecturer in Mental Health Nursing, you will play an important role in preparing future nurses to deliver safe, compassionate and evidence-informed mental health care. Working within a dedicated and collaborative academic team, you will share your clinical expertise and passion for mental health to deliver engaging, contemporary education that develops students’ clinical knowledge, cultural responsiveness and recovery-oriented practice. You will contribute to curriculum development, simulation-based learning, student placements and research, while building partnerships with mental health services and community organisations. This is an opportunity to inspire future nurses, support student success and make a meaningful contribution to mental health nursing education and the wellbeing of individuals and communities. For more information on the School of Health, please visit us online: School of Health You will: deliver high-quality mental health nursing education through engaging teaching, contemporary curriculum development, simulation-based learning and student-centred assessment; contribute to research and scholarship in mental health and wellbeing, including research projects, publications, grant applications and the supervision or co-supervision of higher degree research candidates; and build and maintain productive partnerships with mental health services, healthcare providers, professional networks, community organisations, consumers and carers to strengthen student placements, graduate outcomes and research collaboration. About you You are an experienced mental health nursing clinician with a passion for education and a commitment to preparing future nurses for contemporary mental health practice. You bring a strong understanding of recovery-oriented, person-centred and culturally responsive care, alongside an enthusiasm for translating your clinical expertise into engaging and meaningful learning experiences for students. You are interested in developing your academic career through teaching, research and industry engagement, and value collaboration with colleagues, students and external partners. You will thrive in a supportive and collegial environment where you can contribute to innovative nursing education, strengthen connections with mental health services and make a meaningful contribution to the health and wellbeing of our communities. You will possess: A completed or near-completed doctoral qualification in a relevant field, or equivalent accreditation and standing. Current registration as a nurse with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA), with demonstrated expertise and contemporary clinical experience in mental health nursing. Demonstrated teaching effectiveness, including the ability to develop and deliver engaging higher education curricula that support student satisfaction, learning and success. Evidence of research experience, including refereed publications, participation in research teams or supervision or co-supervision of honours and higher degree research candidates. Membership of and sound connections with relevant mental health professional bodies, community groups and/or professional practice networks. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, a collaborative approach, and a commitment to contributing to a positive academic environment and continually developing your teaching and research capabilities. Desirable Credentialed Mental Health Nurse status, or eligibility for credentialing through the Australian College of Mental Health Nurses (ACMHN). Experience undertaking academic administration, such as course coordination, within a university. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Thursday 12 November 2026. Position description: 494928_Lecturer in Mental Health Nursing.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume, and a response to selection criteria. Noting that within the application form, we will request a statement addressing each of the selection criteria contained within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Professor Stephen Neville Discipline Lead, Nursing – School of Health Email: sneville2@usc.edu.au UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you International Business Development Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Individual contributor, International , L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super, Professional Support UniSC’s international recruitment success by delivering targeted onshore strategies, strengthening education agent partnerships and building pathways that attract international students and convert opportunities into enrolments. Finance Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast Financial Services, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Professional Partner with senior leaders to shape financial decisions that directly support UniSC’s strategy, growth and sustainability. Senior Lecturer in Prosthetics and Orthotics UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic, LC $144,979 - $167,068 +17% super, School of Health An exceptional opportunity to shape the future of prosthetics and orthotics education, advance impactful research, and strengthen partnerships with clinical and industry leaders at a university committed to innovation and real-world impact. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Fraser Coast Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
