    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-in-nursing-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia-unisc-caboolture": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Nursing",
      "description": "Lecturer in Nursing - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Lecturer in Nursing UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia, 4510 UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Academic LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super School of Health Full-Time School of Health | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs or UniSC Caboolture Academic Level B - $118,481 - $140,567 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time, ongoing appointment | Relocation assistance available for eligible candidates SOH: Where Passion Meets Impact - Join the School of Health! Are you eager to make a difference in health education and research? Join our dedicated team of researchers and educators at the School of Health (SOH). We have a strong focus on cultivating healthy minds, bodies, and environments through our teaching, research, and outreach efforts. With a purpose that extends regionally and impacts globally, we are committed to advancing knowledge in the health sector and improving the well-being of our communities. Together, let's create healthier communities now and for the generations to come. The Opportunity As a Lecturer in Nursing, you will play an important role in shaping the next generation of nurses and preparing graduates to thrive in a rapidly evolving healthcare environment. Working alongside a dedicated and collaborative academic team, you will deliver engaging, contemporary learning experiences that connect theory with practice, support student success and contribute to exceptional graduate outcomes. This is an opportunity to share your nursing expertise, inspire future healthcare professionals and make a meaningful difference to the quality of nursing education. You will also contribute to research, strengthen partnerships with healthcare providers and industry, and expand work-integrated learning opportunities that prepare students for real-world clinical and community settings. Relocation assistance is available for eligible candidates, offering an opportunity to grow your academic career while contributing to healthier communities across Queensland. For more information on the School of Health, please visit us online: School of Health You will: deliver high-quality nursing education through engaging teaching, contemporary curriculum development and student-centred learning experiences; contribute to research projects, scholarly publications and grant applications while developing your research profile and supporting honours and higher degree research candidates; and build productive partnerships with healthcare providers, professional networks and community organisations to strengthen work-integrated learning, graduate outcomes and the student experience. About you You are a passionate nursing professional and emerging academic who is committed to delivering an exceptional student experience and preparing graduates for the realities of contemporary healthcare. You bring a student-centred approach to teaching, an interest in developing your research career and a genuine enthusiasm for working collaboratively with colleagues, students and industry partners. You value continuous learning, enjoy sharing your clinical and academic expertise, and are motivated by the opportunity to connect education with real-world health outcomes. You will thrive in a supportive and collegial environment where you can continue to grow as an academic while contributing to the future of nursing education. You will possess: A completed or near-completed doctoral qualification in a relevant field, or equivalent accreditation and standing. Current registration as a nurse with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA). Demonstrated teaching effectiveness, including the ability to develop and deliver engaging higher education curricula and support positive student outcomes. Evidence of research experience, including publications, participation in research projects, grant applications or supervision of honours and higher degree research candidates. Established connections with relevant professional bodies, healthcare providers, community groups and/or professional practice networks. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, a collaborative approach, and a commitment to ongoing academic development and continuous improvement in teaching and research. Desirable Experience undertaking academic administration, such as course coordination, within a university. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Tuesday 10 November 2026. Position description: 494929_Lecturer in Nursing.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume, and a response to selection criteria. Noting that within the application form, we will request a statement addressing each of the selection criteria contained within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Professor Stephen Neville Discipline Lead, Nursing – School of Health Email: sneville2@usc.edu.au UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you International Business Development Coordinator UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Moreton Bay Individual contributor, International , L6 $95,986 - $103,873 +17% super, Professional Support UniSC’s international recruitment success by delivering targeted onshore strategies, strengthening education agent partnerships and building pathways that attract international students and convert opportunities into enrolments. Finance Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast Financial Services, L7 $105,843 - $115,703 +17% super, Professional Partner with senior leaders to shape financial decisions that directly support UniSC’s strategy, growth and sustainability. Senior Lecturer in Prosthetics and Orthotics UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic, LC $144,979 - $167,068 +17% super, School of Health An exceptional opportunity to shape the future of prosthetics and orthotics education, advance impactful research, and strengthen partnerships with clinical and industry leaders at a university committed to innovation and real-world impact. Technician (Nursing and Midwifery) UniSC Fraser Coast Academic Support Unit, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super, Technical Support Join a growing UniSC team, with multiple newly created opportunities supporting the expansion of our Nursing and Midwifery programs. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
